  "name": "housekeeping: gitignore .lock.stale-* sentinels; launcher double-spawn; takeover transcript gap; unbounded notes; events defaults",
  "slug": "housekeeping-gitignore-lock-stale",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "housekeeping: gitignore .lock.stale-* sentinels; launcher double-spawn; takeover transcript gap; unbounded notes; events defaults",
    "details_md": "Grab-bag of small confirmed items: (1) .gitignore covers .lock and .tmp-* but not the .lock.stale-<token> sentinels the stale-breaker can leave (lock.ts:281). (2) bin/slop.mjs spawns bun --version before every real run — measurable startup tax; try the real spawn and map ENOENT instead. (3) takeover/review re-entry end sessions without transcript capture while docs/configuration.md:110 claims capture on every end — fix docs or add best-effort capture. (4) --note/--outcome/--reason unbounded (done --outcome - reads all stdin) — consider caps. (5) slop events with no flags returns the whole log and next_cursor:null when everything is elided though has_more:true — give events a default limit and always emit a usable cursor.",
    "acceptance": [
      "each sub-item fixed or explicitly wontfixed"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/repo/lock.ts:281",
      "bin/slop.mjs",
      "docs/configuration.md:110",
      "src/cli/commands/events.ts"
    ],
